{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-03 finite-pass fuse decision APPROVED (2026-08-17). Retain only the scoped three-consecutive arm; remove the rolling five-of-ten arm. Endpoint-family scope opens after 3 consecutive exhausted eligible logical outcomes across at least 2 tickets. Provider scope uses the same threshold and additionally requires at least 2 independent endpoint families. A matching successful logical outcome resets the consecutive counter. Physical attempts, recovered fallbacks, permanent ticket failures, and opaque unclassified diagnostics do not count. Authoritative auth/configuration/quota/rate-limit/per-issue signals retain their direct scopes.\n\nRationale: three exhausted logical outcomes can represent up to nine physical provider calls under the approved envelope, while the five-of-ten arm has neither maintained-Jira precedent nor historical Rebar calibration and could discard useful progress from an alternating success/failure batch. Current Rebar often aborts earlier based on exception representation, so the approved normalized fuse is more permissive and consistent.\n\nHistorical evidence status: the completed 1,200-run replay slice produced zero approved-fuse openings and zero premature stops; targeted incidents confirm that healed warnings, ticket-local 404s, opaque ACLI errors, and authoritative credential failures must not feed inferred outage state. Full replay of all 415 failed runs and remaining successful slices remains evidence-completion work, not an unresolved design decision. Local record updated: `.joe-janitor/rp03-fuse-history-validation.md`. No tracked or production file changed; RP-04 remains untouched."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787021743005388001,"uuid":"bad76979-110e-40fa-bb25-a41c14503123"}